    "description": {
      "en": "This is the employee PRSI Class A contribution rate (4.1% in the latest system) applied to gross employee earnings above the €38/week exemption threshold. It is used as the 'formula' parameter of the ArithOp function in tscee_ie commented 'PRSI Class A: pre-credit contribution (per month in work)', multiplying eligible earnings to produce the pre-credit contribution before the tapered PRSI credit is netted off. Both sources confirm this rate: the country report's Table 10 shows the Class A employee rate at 4% for 2022-2024 rising to 4.1% for 2025, and the theme document confirms 4.1% for 2025 (rising further to 4.2% in 2026, a change not yet reflected in this constant's latest value)."
